# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working
# tree on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. The test suite pins source files by slicing
# them between literal anchors and by sha256 of exact byte ranges - for example
# the GEV_REALTIME_TOOLS schema pin, which asserts a 31104-byte block. On a
# Windows checkout with autocrlf, every one of those anchors misses and the byte
# lengths drift by one per line. Measured on this repo: 25 of 2587 tests fail
# with CRLF, and 0 fail with LF. The failures look like real regressions and are
# not, which is worse than a plain breakage.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is the load-bearing part: it forces LF into the
# working tree, so the files the test runner actually reads are LF regardless of
# core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers. Left CRLF because they are read by Windows tooling,
# never by the test suite. The .ps1 files additionally carry a UTF-8 BOM, which
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 needs to avoid decoding them as ANSI - see app/README.md.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.glb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.wav binary
